WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.875
A tidy report is easier to build and easier to read.

2
00:00:04.875 --> 00:00:10.061
In this lesson, you will learn how a card summarizes a field by default,

3
00:00:10.061 --> 00:00:15.247
how to keep all your measures in one table, and how to organize your

4
00:00:15.247 --> 00:00:17.840
report into named pages. Let's get organized!

5
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.940
Here I dropped the Product field into a card.

6
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:25.820
The card shows fifty percent Dark Bites. Why?

7
00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:30.140
For a text field, a card shows the first value by default.

8
00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:32.300
This is called an implicit summary.

9
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.177
Implicit summaries can mislead readers.

10
00:00:43.177 --> 00:00:49.108
So instead, we will write our own measures, and control exactly what each card shows.

11
00:00:49.108 --> 00:00:51.480
I delete this card for now.

12
00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:55.609
In the Data pane, we have the tables we loaded:

13
00:00:55.609 --> 00:00:58.220
Calendar, Geo, Product, Sales Person, and Shipments.

14
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:19.035
Measures can live in any table, but they are easier to find in one place.

15
00:01:19.035 --> 00:01:23.226
So I create an empty table with Enter data, and name it Formula.

16
00:01:23.226 --> 00:01:25.160
All our measures will go here.

17
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.380
Click Load, and the Formula table appears at the top of the Data pane.

18
00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.382
Next, the pages.

19
00:01:50.382 --> 00:01:55.899
At the bottom, I rename Page one to Statistical, and add pages for Filter,

20
00:01:55.899 --> 00:01:57.870
Logic, and Date and Time.

21
00:01:57.870 --> 00:01:59.840
One page for each topic.

22
00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.526
Now the report has a clear structure.

23
00:02:19.526 --> 00:02:23.180
Every measure has a home, and every topic has a page.

24
00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.888
Plan your report before you build it.

25
00:02:51.888 --> 00:02:54.960
Good structure saves hours later. Let's start building!

